    "code": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    S = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n    n = len(S)\n    # Greedy: scan with current position index in final string\n    pos = 0\n    inserts = 0\n    # We can insert 'i' at odd positions and 'o' at even positions.\n    # For each character in S, we must align it to the correct parity.\n    for c in S:\n        # expected parity: character must be at position with index pos\n        # pos is index in final string (0-based), odd positions are 0,2,...\n        expected = 'i' if (pos % 2 == 0) else 'o'\n        if c != expected:\n            # Need to insert characters to change pos parity so that c lands on its needed parity.\n            # If c == 'i', it needs pos even. If pos is odd, insert one 'o'? Wait, inserting chars before c changes pos.\n            # Let's instead decide minimal inserts before c.\n            # If c == 'i', it must be at even final index. If current pos is odd, insert one char ('o')? But inserting changes pos by 1.\n            # If c == 'o', it must be at odd final index. If current pos is even, insert one char ('i').\n            # But we also need inserted chars to be valid (alternate). Since final string is fixed pattern, insertions must fill pattern.\n            # Simpler: maintain pattern; count insertions required to make next original char fit.\n            # Expected char at current pos is expected.\n            # We need c to be placed at the first position where pattern matches c.\n            # If current pos already matches c's parity, no insert.\n            # Otherwise insert (number of pattern chars needed) until pos parity matches c.\n            if c == 'i' and pos % 2 == 1:\n                # Need one insert to move to even pos; insert char at current pos (must be 'o' since odd pos? 0-based odd means final 2nd char 'o')\n                inserts += 1\n                pos += 1\n            elif c == 'o' and pos % 2 == 0:\n                inserts += 1\n                pos += 1\n        # Place c\n        pos += 1\n    # Now pos is total length (number of chars). Must be even. If odd, insert one 'o' at end.\n    if pos % 2 == 1:\n        inserts += 1\n        pos += 1\n    print(inserts)\n\nmain()",
